---
// design/14_DATA.md. Route built, deliberately unlinked — design/14 itself states a qualified
// data-protection solicitor must review this page before it is linked anywhere, and
// instructions/BLOCK_1_COMPONENTS.md is explicit that /data is linked only from /contact, and
// only once that review is done. Neither the nav nor Footer.astro nor contact.astro link here
// (Footer's own premature link was found and removed at task 3.6). No retention/deletion
// commitment below is softened or summarised — transcribed in full, per this task's own
// instruction.
//
// The DPA CTA and contact address use the site's established "[REPLACE WITH DOMAIN EMAIL
// BEFORE LAUNCH]" placeholder rather than design/14's own literal "contact@oxiedo.com" — the
// company name itself is an open decision (see /faq "Why is this called Oxiedo?"), so treating
// "oxiedo.com" as a confirmed domain here would be inconsistent with that. design/14's internal
// -only legal note ("do not publish this blockquote") is correctly omitted.
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../components/Eyebrow.astro';
---

<Page title="DATA HANDLING POLICY">
	<section class="section container">
		<Eyebrow>DATA HANDLING POLICY</Eyebrow>
		<h1>What happens to your data. Stated completely.</h1>
		<p class="data-updated tabular">Last updated: September 2026 · Version 1.0</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal">
		<h2>The short version</h2>
		<p class="data-prose">
			We receive your data. We run the diagnostic. We return the report. We delete your
			data.
		</p>
		<p class="data-prose">
			We do not retain, sell, use to train, publish, or share your data without your
			explicit written permission. Period.
		</p>
		<p class="data-prose">
			If you want the long version — for procurement, legal review, or your own peace of
			mind — it is below.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal">
		<h2>What data we handle</h2>
		<p class="data-prose"><strong>For The Proofreader:</strong></p>
		<ul class="data-list">
			<li>Your model checkpoint (read-only — we do not modify the weights)</li>
			<li>Your labelled dataset</li>
			<li>Data source columns, if provided</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="data-prose"><strong>For The Warning Light:</strong></p>
		<ul class="data-list">
			<li>Access to a training run (logs, gradients, checkpoints at each step)</li>
			<li>No ongoing access after the engagement ends</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="data-prose"><strong>For The Diary:</strong></p>
		<ul class="data-list">
			<li>Training telemetry from a run conducted in or with the ORMAS engine</li>
			<li>The modification record generated by that run</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="data-prose"><strong>We do not request:</strong></p>
		<ul class="data-list">
			<li>Personal data about your employees</li>
			<li>Customer data beyond what is necessary for the diagnostic</li>
			<li>Credentials, API keys, or production system access</li>
			<li>Any data not directly relevant to the diagnostic question</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal">
		<h2>How we handle it</h2>

		<h3 class="data-subheading">Storage</h3>
		<p class="data-prose">
			Your data is stored on encrypted storage for the duration of the engagement only.
			Encryption at rest: AES-256. Encryption in transit: TLS 1.3. Storage location: [TO BE
			CONFIRMED — EU-based for EU customers, or in your own environment for on-premise
			engagements].
		</p>

		<h3 class="data-subheading">Access</h3>
		<p class="data-prose">
			Access is restricted to the person(s) running the diagnostic. For the current
			engagement, that means one person: Rokib Al Dhin Raadh. This will be updated as the
			team grows.
		</p>
		<p class="data-prose">No third party has access to your data except:</p>
		<ul class="data-list">
			<li>Cloud infrastructure providers (storage, compute) under their own DPAs</li>
			<li>Legal or professional advisors under confidentiality obligations, if required</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="data-prose">
			We will name any infrastructure provider used for your specific engagement before
			work begins.
		</p>

		<h3 class="data-subheading">Retention</h3>
		<p class="data-prose">
			Your data is deleted within 30 days of the diagnostic report being delivered. On
			request, we can confirm deletion in writing, including the storage location wiped and
			the method used.
		</p>
		<p class="data-prose">We retain:</p>
		<ul class="data-list">
			<li>The diagnostic report itself (indefinitely, unless you request deletion)</li>
			<li>
				Aggregate findings that do not identify your organisation or your model (e.g., "in
				one engagement, the architecture identified 12% label noise in a 50,000-example
				dataset" — no names, no identifying information)
			</li>
			<li>Internal correspondence related to the engagement</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="data-prose">We do not retain:</p>
		<ul class="data-list">
			<li>Your model checkpoint after 30 days</li>
			<li>Your dataset after 30 days</li>
			<li>Your run logs after 30 days</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal">
		<h2>What we will never do</h2>
		<ul class="data-never-list">
			<li>We will not use your data to train any model, including ORMAS.</li>
			<li>We will not share your data with any third party for commercial purposes.</li>
			<li>
				We will not publish any result that identifies your organisation without your
				explicit written permission.
			</li>
			<li>We will not sell, license, or transfer your data.</li>
			<li>
				We will not access your data after the engagement ends, except for the retention
				items listed above.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal">
		<h2>On-premise option</h2>
		<p class="data-prose">
			If your data cannot leave your environment — for regulatory, security, or policy
			reasons — we offer an on-premise engagement mode. You run the diagnostic engine in
			your own infrastructure. We provide the tooling, support the run remotely, and receive
			only the output (the report). No model checkpoint, dataset, or run log ever leaves
			your environment.
		</p>
		<p class="data-prose">
			This is the standard mode for any engagement involving clinical, financial, or
			classified data. Tell us in the booking form if this is required.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal">
		<h2>Legal basis and jurisdiction</h2>
		<p class="data-prose">
			We are incorporated in England and Wales (company number: [TBD]). Data handling is
			governed by UK GDPR and the UK Data Protection Act 2018.
		</p>
		<p class="data-prose">
			For EU-based customers, we operate under the same principles and, where required,
			under EU GDPR via standard contractual clauses.
		</p>
		<p class="data-prose">
			For financial and medical data, applicable sector-specific regulations take
			precedence. We will confirm the applicable framework for your engagement before work
			begins.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal">
		<h2>Data Processing Agreement (DPA)</h2>
		<p class="data-prose">
			Any engagement involving personal data or regulated data requires a signed Data
			Processing Agreement before work begins. We do not start an engagement without one.
		</p>
		<p class="data-prose">
			A template DPA is available on request. If you require your own form, send it to us
			for review.
		</p>
		<p class="data-cta">Request the DPA template: [REPLACE WITH DOMAIN EMAIL BEFORE LAUNCH]</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal">
		<h2>Contact for data queries</h2>
		<p class="data-prose">
			Data-related questions, DPA requests, deletion requests, and breach reports:
		</p>
		<p class="data-cta">[REPLACE WITH DOMAIN EMAIL BEFORE LAUNCH]</p>
		<p class="data-prose">Subject: "Data handling — [your organisation name]"</p>
		<p class="data-prose">We respond to data-related queries within 5 business days.</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal">
		<h2>What this page does not cover</h2>
		<p class="data-prose">This page covers data handling during an engagement. It does not cover:</p>
		<ul class="data-list">
			<li>Website analytics (we intend to use none, or privacy-preserving only)</li>
			<li>Contact form data (stored in our email, not shared, deleted on request)</li>
			<li>The terms of the engagement contract (see the terms provided before each engagement)</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="data-prose">If you have a question not covered here, write to us.</p>
	</section>
</Page>
